1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,070
We have so much stuff to carry around these days – mobile phones, keys, credit cards and laptops.
如今我们有太多东西要随身携带——手机、钥匙、信用卡和笔记本电脑。

2
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:15,400
Some of us might stuff them into various pockets in our clothes and others will put them in a bag.
我们中的一些人可能会把它们塞进衣服的各个口袋里，而另一些人则会把它们放在包里。

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,250
For women this might be a practical and trendy handbag.
对女性来说，这可能是一个实用又时髦的（trendy）手提包。

4
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:24,880
But how are men supposed to carry things around and look cool?
但男性要怎么携带东西又看起来很酷呢？

5
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,550
The answer is a manbag!
答案是男士包！

6
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:34,930
They are the height of fashion at the moment – a stylish accessory that modern men are carrying around.
它们目前是最流行的——一种现代男性随身携带的时尚配饰。

7
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:46,330
I'm a little cynical about these must-have items – let's face it, a manbag by any other name is a bag and I have one - my trusty backpack.
我对这些必备品有点愤世嫉俗（cynical）——面对现实吧，不管叫什么，男士包就是个包，而且我就有一个——我可靠的双肩背包。

8
00:00:46,330 --> 00:01:01,650
However, senior fashion analyst for market research company Mintel, Tamara Senders, describes a manbag as "a bag worn by men, including backpacks and other styles such as shoulder bags."
然而，市场研究公司英敏特（Mintel）的高级时尚分析师塔玛拉・森德斯（Tamara Senders）将男士包描述为“男性背的包，包括背包以及其他款式，如肩包”。

9
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:14,730
I can't see my old backpack being a style icon, but maybe I'm just not on-trend: According to Mintel, 15 per cent of men bought one in the UK last year.
我不觉得我的旧背包会成为时尚标志，但也许我只是跟不上潮流：据英敏特的数据，去年在英国，15%的男性购买了男士包。

10
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:18,200
Maybe it's the name that's putting me off.
也许是这个名字让我反感。

11
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,080
Why does a bag have to have a gender?
为什么包还要分性别呢？

12
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:27,540
I suppose they're being marketed as a stylish fashion item designed to look good on men.
我想它们正在被当作专为男性设计、看起来很有型的时尚单品来推销。

13
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:31,570
I've heard that many big names have flocked to adopt the trend.
我听说很多名人都热衷于追随这一潮流。

14
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:38,760
Pharrell Williams, David Beckham and Kanye West, are just some of those who've been spotted rocking a manbag.
法瑞尔・威廉姆斯（Pharrell Williams）、大卫・贝克汉姆（David Beckham）和坎耶・维斯特（Kanye West），只是被看到背男士包名人中的一部分。

15
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:44,990
My reservations about being seen carrying one may be down to my Britishness.
我对被人看到背着男士包有所顾虑，这可能归因于我是英国人。

16
00:01:44,990 --> 00:02:00,140
According to Nick Carvell, the Contributing Fashion Editor for GQ magazine: "In Britain we are still very tied up with that idea of masculinity that is almost so fragile that it can be dented by carrying a bag."
据《GQ》杂志特约时尚编辑尼克・卡维尔（Nick Carvell）说：“在英国，我们仍然非常纠结于那种男子气概的观念，这种观念几乎如此脆弱，以至于背个包都能被削弱。”

17
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:11,740
So, while some British men might think a manbag to be effeminate and not very 'macho', he thinks that many Europeans don't have an issue with toting such a fashionable item.
所以，虽然一些英国男性可能认为男士包娘娘腔（effeminate），不太有“男子气概”（macho），但他认为很多欧洲人对携带（toting）这样一个时尚单品并不在意。

18
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:18,860
Of course, if I was to exchange my old backpack for a manbag, it would come at a price.
当然，如果我要用旧背包换一个男士包，那可得付出一定的代价（花高价）。

19
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:28,020
With people like Louis Vuitton, Fendi, Gucci and Dolce and Gabbana designing these bags, they can come with a hefty price tag.
像路易威登（Louis Vuitton）、芬迪（Fendi）、古驰（Gucci）和杜嘉班纳（Dolce and Gabbana）这些品牌所设计出来的包，价格可能会很高昂（hefty）。

20
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,900
I suppose that's the price of fashion!
我想这就是时尚的代价！

21
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:40,760
And apparently, if I had any spare cash, I could complete my designer outfit by buying a murse – that's a man's purse!
而且显然，如果我有闲钱，我可以买一个murse来搭配我的设计师潮服——也就是男士用的钱包！

22
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:52,120
I suppose fashions change and we have come a long way from the days when men carried their things in a very masculine briefcase - sturdy, sensible and practical.
我想时尚在变化，男性用非常有男子气概，结实、朴素又实用的公文包来装东西的那个时代已经过去了很久。

23
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:58,940
Now, it seems, we have to put as much thought into buying a bag as we do into buying our clothes.
现在，似乎我们在买包时要像买衣服一样深思熟虑。
